}
```
Wait stage might be centered but with space-between: topbar at start, main containing cabinet at middle, touch at end. `.stage-wrap` includes cabinet and hints (hidden). `main` is middle child. With `justify-content:space-between`, topbar top, main center? Actually free space distributed equally between children: topbar at top, main after first gap, touch bottom. Since main has no flex-grow, it sits at 1/2 of free space? With three items and space-between, second item is at (container - item2 - item3 - ...)? Let's compute: items topbar 30, main 344, touch 76, gaps each (844-450)/2=197. So topbar at 10, gap197, main at 237, gap197, touch at 658. Stage y ~237 vs current 273. Not much difference, and touch at bottom. That's nice. Empty between. Stage remains similar. Fine.

But perhaps we want stage larger. Keep 94vw. Stage 367x344.

Landscape:
