content.text:
Landscape: controls below stage, stage small in center, huge empty sides. Could in landscape place controls at left/right sides of stage to use horizontal space and enlarge stage vertically. On phones landscape, typical layout has controls overlay left/right and game center filling height. Our current stage height 258 leaves topbar 52 and controls 58; total 390. Could enlarge stage by using height better: stage width limited by `(100dvh - 132px)` = 258, but if controls were side overlays, we could use `(100dvh - 70px)` = 320 height => width 341. Or even 100dvh-40 => 373, but topbar. The sides have 284px margins, perfect for controls.

Better responsive landscape:
- Put touch controls position fixed/absolute at left and right sides, vertically centered, while stage max width based on height. Since `.touch` direct child of app, can reposition in landscape: `.touch { position: fixed; inset: 0; width:100%; min-height:0; pointer-events:none; display:flex; }` pads absolute at sides; buttons pointer auto. But if it overlays the stage, pads at far sides won't overlap due margins. Set `.touch-left{position:absolute;left:12px;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%)}` and right similarly; but these classes currently have no positioning. Add in media.
- Stage width in landscape: `min(760px, calc((100dvh - 68px) * 256/240))` and maybe width 70vw; controls on sides. For 844x390: height 390-68=322 -> width 343; stage 343x322. Topbar at top 30; stage y maybe 45; bottom 367. Controls at left/right center around y=195. This fills better.
- But topbar brand at top center, stage center. Good.
- The touch controls absolute fixed to viewport over sides. Body no scroll.

Would be nicer for landscape. Let's implement landscape media:
```
@media (max-height:520px) and (orientation:landscape){
 .app{--stage-w: min(84vw, calc((100dvh - 74px)*256/240)); justify-content:center; gap:6px; padding...}
 .topbar{width:var(--stage-w)}
 .touch{position:fixed;left:0;right:0;top:0;bottom:0;width:auto;min-height:0;max-width:none;pointer-events:none;display:none;} // but body.touch-mode display:flex
 .touch-pad{position:absolute;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);}
 .touch-left{left:max(16px, env(safe-area-inset-left));}
 .touch-right{right:max(16px, env(safe-area-inset-right));}
 .tbtn{ width:60px;height:60px;}
 .tbtn.a{width:68px;height:68px;}
 .tbtn.b{margin-bottom:0}
}
```
But `.touch` display flex from body.touch-mode; with position fixed and children absolute, fine. However `.touch` width/height auto and inset 0. `body.touch-mode .touch {display:flex}` applies. In landscape controls at far sides, left/right. The `.touch-pad` flex, B/A side by side; right pad at right. Good. The stage width 84vw max => 709, but height cap 322 => 343. So stage 343 wide centered, sides ~250 each; controls occupy ~140 each. Good.

Topbar+stage: stage height 322 + topbar 30 + gap ~6 = 358, center vertical in 390 => 16 top. stage y~52. Controls at mid 195. Good.

Need ensure stage doesn't overlap controls: controls left 16..~150, stage x=(844-343)/2=250.5, safe. Right controls x~690..828, stage ends 593. Good.

This makes landscape much better. Let's implement. Also title instructions change.

First title text mobile.

